# SRG-APP-000516-AU-000350  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must be configured to notify the System
# Administrator (SA) and Information System Security Officer (ISSO), at a
# minimum, when an attack is detected on multiple devices and hosts within
# its scope of coverage.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000516-AU-000350
group:           V-206514
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000366
control_rev5:    CM-6

contribution:    Splunk can run a detection search on a schedule and send its result to
                 named recipients by email, so the notification path and the people on it
                 are expressed in the application's own configuration.

governs:         alert_actions.conf - What Splunk does when an alert fires, such as sending email or calling a
                 webhook.
governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.

check:           savedsearches.conf [] enableSched equals 1
check:           savedsearches.conf [] cron_schedule non_empty
check:           savedsearches.conf [] action.email in 1|true
check:           savedsearches.conf [] action.email.to non_empty
check:           alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver not_equals localhost
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver non_empty -> alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver not_equals localhost
vendor:          alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.3-configuration-file-reference/alert_actions.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Who the SA and ISSO are and what detection logic constitutes an attack
                 across multiple devices, both organization-defined; the product STIG
                 verifies this part by interviewing the SA and confirming receipt with the
                 ISSO rather than by reading configuration (SPLK-CL-000280 check text).
external:        Delivery of the message, carried by the mail transfer agent and the
                 network.
external:        Where analysis is performed by another device, the benchmark marks the
                 requirement not applicable, which is a deployment-design determination.

citation:        Central Log Server SRG SRG-APP-000516-AU-000350 check text; SPLK-CL-000280
                 check and fix text; savedsearches.conf.spec:73 (enableSched = [0 | 1],
                 default 0), savedsearches.conf.spec:79 (cron_schedule),
                 savedsearches.conf.spec:300 (action.email, default false),
                 savedsearches.conf.spec:304 (action.email.to, REQUIRED),
                 alert_actions.conf.spec:276 (mailserver)
finding:         No scheduled search carries an enabled email action with a recipient list
                 and a reachable mail server, so the application cannot notify anyone when
                 a detection fires across multiple hosts.
